# family: liveness
# bridge: B(lifecycle-trace)
# regime: exact (names and integers, no tolerance)
# instrument-first: a90f998f7cd0
# baseline: tests/unit/liveness, tests/integration/liveness
# baseline-count: 54
# added-count: 1
#
# The unit is NetwLivenessCore, which was already native, and the record half
# of LivenessShell, which is now part of it.
#
# THIS IS A PARTIAL CROSSING AND THE ROWS SAY SO: ported=0. The class crossed
# and the specification did not, because all 54 cases drive the shell that
# survives until W6. A ledger with no ported row is not a formality here. It is
# the honest reading of a family whose suites were never pointed at the thing
# that moved, and writing it down is what stops a later session from concluding
# that liveness never crossed at all.
#
# THE RECIPE RECONCILIATION, which §5 W2 left open. "The batch ports the
# shell's record half" is a smaller claim than "a class migrates completely or
# not at all", and both are satisfied, because LivenessShell was never one
# class's worth of concern. It is two planes sharing a file:
#
#   record plane   routes, states, the waiting room, the frame counter
#                  holds no Object, so it outlives every entity it names
#   wrapper plane  NetwEntity, the node hooks, the session, the entity-typed
#                  signals -- every one of them an Object
#
# The RECORD plane migrated completely. After this batch liveness_shell.gd
# holds no record state at all: `core` is the native store, `_api_ref` is the
# session, and `_entities` is the wrapper cache. There is nothing left in it
# that does not touch an Object, so no class straddles the two tiers and the
# recipe's rule holds on the class that actually crossed.
#
# O7 (RID-typed liveness signal forms) IS TAKEN HERE, AND IT IS REFUSED. The
# obvious move is for the core to emit route_live(route, entity) / route_
# lingering / route_dead with the shell re-emitting its NetwEntity-typed forms
# on top. A law the record plane already has defeats it: bind_routes_data emits
# nothing per route ON PURPOSE, because a wave of two thousand rows carries no
# wrapper any listener could reach through. A record-plane signal would have to
# fire on every bind_route, those two thousand included, or carry a per-call
# flag asking whether to announce this one -- and a signal you have to ask for
# is not a signal anyone can build on. So the announcement stays where the
# thing announced is meaningful, entity-typed on the wrapper plane, and it
# crosses with the shell at W6. This is EntityDecl's disposition at the table
# batch applied to a second family: public surface with no consumer is refused
# rather than deferred.
#
# WHY EVERY CASE CARRIES, measured rather than assumed. Not one of the 54 is
# core-direct the way the table family's two wire suites were. test_liveness_
# core.gd reads api=0 tree=0 and looks like a duplicate of the native laws; it
# is not. Its cases assert NetwLivenessCore.STATE_* == LivenessShell.State.* ==
# NetwMultiplayer.EntityState.*, which is a cross-implementation seam check
# only GDScript can make, and it dies with the shell rather than with this
# batch.
#
# THE INSTRUMENT is tests/crossing/liveness_arm.gd against
# tests/native/goldens/liveness_lifecycle.txt: 45 rows over 8 scenarios,
# recorded from the GDScript record plane at a90f998f before a line of it was
# native, and red-proven twice against planted nonconformers (a sweep off by
# one poll, and a bulk door minting past a record a wrapper already held).
# The golden's `record/` half is replayed natively by liveness_trace_tests.cpp
# and its `shell/` half stays the arm's to check until the shell goes.
#
# G4 named extension/tests/data/ as the goldens' home. Neither crossing used
# it. Both goldens live under res://tests/native/goldens/ and both consuming
# cases are Tier 2a, because that is the tier that can read a project path.
#
# WHAT THE FAMILY GAINED NATIVELY, named so the next census delta is
# attributable. Six cases, none of them a successor to a row below:
#   liveness_core_tests.cpp  "[Networked][Liveness][Hosted] L6 the bulk door mints an identity per route and lands on one already standing"
#   liveness_core_tests.cpp  "[Networked][Liveness][Hosted] L7 a wait is answered once, by the binding that made its route live"
#   liveness_core_tests.cpp  "[Networked][Liveness][Hosted] L8 a wait expires against the counter it was armed on"
#   liveness_core_tests.cpp  "[Networked][Liveness][Hosted] L9 one expiry does not take its route's other waits with it"
#   liveness_core_tests.cpp  "[Networked][Liveness][Hosted] L10 a wait armed on a clock ignores the frame counter"
#   liveness_trace_tests.cpp "[Networked][Liveness] the native record plane reproduces the recorded lifecycle trace"
#
